From: Toon Verwaest <verwaest@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:03:01 +0200
Subject: [parser] Validate non-arrow call arguments as expressions

In ParserBase::ParseArguments, each argument is parsed using
ParseAssignmentExpressionCoverGrammar() inside an AccumulationScope.
Previously, ClassifyArrowParameter(&accumulation_scope, ...) was only
called when maybe_arrow == kMaybeArrowHead. When maybe_arrow ==
kNotArrowHead, pending expression errors (such as an invalid
CoverInitializedName `{x = z}`) were neither validated nor accumulated
before parsing subsequent arguments, allowing a later destructuring
assignment argument (e.g. `f({x = z}, [a] = [])`) to clear the
expression error via ValidateAsPattern().

Call accumulation_scope.ValidateExpression() for each argument when
maybe_arrow != kMaybeArrowHead so expression errors are immediately
reported and pattern errors from inside the argument are cleared.

